<div class="page">
    <h2 style="font-size: 18pt;">3 Criteria.</h2>
    <p>Places are allocated on the basis of the following criteria:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Career background 20%: Particular attention is paid to previous education and certificates obtained, general professional development, and applicants' academic and professional goals.</li>
        <li>Written entrance exam 30%: The written entrance exam (English, Mathematics/Statistics, Fundamentals of Business Administration) is designed to test your aptitude for the program.</li>
        <li>Interview 50%: The interview gives you the opportunity to present yourself personally, to expand on the information provided in the application and to explain your academic and professional goals. A Skype-based interview is also possible.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">3.1 Career Background.</h3>
    <p>A key element in the admission process is an assessment of your career background based on the submitted application. A focus is set on the educational, personal and professional achievements as well as on the outlined study and career aspirations. Please add any certificates to prove your career background.</p>

    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">3.2 Written Entrance Exam.</h3>
    <p>The examination consists of three parts (English, Business Studies, and Mathematics/Statistics). The exams are taken online and start on a given date and time. They are available for 24 hours. You will receive an access code a few days prior to the examination. This access code enables you to open the exam website and participate in the examination. Once you logged in, you have access to all three exams. You can choose with which exam they want to start, however, as soon as one exam is opened, you have exactly 60 minutes to complete it. Please note that the time cannot be stopped. This is true for each part of the examination.</p>
    <p>You can find a video tutorial for the exam software here: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nlbx5a3ls" data-field="exam_tutorial_link">{{ exam_tutorial_link }}</a></p>
    <p>The following standard installations are required on the computer in order to access the examination paper:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Browser: Firefox 1.5 or higher</li>
        <li>PDF: Acrobat Reader 5.0 or higher</li>
        <li>Office: Word 7.0 (Office 95) or higher</li>
    </ul>

