<div class="page">
    <p>A stable internet connection is crucial in order to complete the examination properly. If that cannot be ensured at home, applicants are advised to go to a university, library or another public place where the condition is given.</p>
    <p>Please note: The online examination has to be completed individually. Taking the exam in groups or letting another person take the exam for you is regarded as cheating and may result in being excluded from the admission procedure.</p>

    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">English</h3>
    <p>The English part of the written exam will take 60 min. The exam consists of a part where applicants will have to prove their competence regarding reading lexical and collocational knowledge. Furthermore, their ability to understand and express opinions about business specific articles will be tested.</p>
    <p>Here are some hints on how to prepare for the exam:</p>
    <p>Read quality newspapers (e.g., the Herald Tribune, Financial Times, Economist, Newsweek) Grammar: Thomson and Martinet: A Practical English Grammar</p>

    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">Mathematics/Statistics</h3>
    <p>The Mathematics/Statistics part of the exam will take 60 min. The exam covers questions regarding arithmetic, algebra, geometry and word problems concerning:</p>
    <p>Fractions: linear, square and exponential functions; calculations including powers; differential and integral calculus; logarithms; expressions with extreme values; roots; descriptive statistics; algebraic transformations; probability calculation; equations and inequalities; binomial and normal distribution</p>
    <p>Here are some hints on how to prepare for the exam:</p>
    <p>Graduate Management Admission Council (2009). GMAT review: The official guide for GMAT review; the only study guide with more than 800 past GMAT questions and their answers by the creators of the test (12. ed.). Chichester, West Sussex: Wiley.</p>

    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">Fundamentals of Business Administration</h3>
    <p>The Business Studies part will take 60 min. The exam will ask for applicant's knowledge concerning basic economic and business principles.</p>
    <p>Here are some hints on how to prepare for the exam:</p>
    <p>In order to prepare for the exam applicants are advised to keep themselves informed about recent economic issues (e.g., Economist, Herald Tribune, Financial Times, Newsweek etc.) and to make sure they understand basic economic relations and business situations. For preparation purposes, applicants will receive articles approximately one week before the written aptitude test takes place.</p>

