<div class="page">
    <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">3.3 Test Examples.</h3>
    <p>Here are some examples of how questions for the online test can look like.</p>

    <p>Examination Subject: English</p>
    <p>Time allowed: 60 minutes – the number of questions for the entire test varies from 30-60 questions, depending on the difficulty.</p>
    <p>Example:</p>
    <p>Complete the following sentence with the correct option:</p>
    <p>We'll have to be very careful how we <span data-field="english_example_1.verb">{{ verb_option_1 }}</span> such a small budget.</p>
    <p>A.) supervise</p>
    <p>B.) allocate</p>
    <p>C.) finance</p>

    <p>Examination Subject: Mathematics/Statistics</p>
    <p>Time allowed: 60 minutes – the number of questions for the entire test varies from 30-60 questions, depending on the difficulty.</p>
    <p>Example:</p>
    <p>Which of the following CANNOT be the greatest common divisor of two positive integers x and y?</p>
    <p>A.) 1</p>
    <p>B.) x</p>
    <p>C.) y</p>
    <p>D.) x+y</p>
    <p>E.) x*y</p>

    <p>Examination Subject: Business Studies</p>
    <p>Time allowed: 60 minutes – the number of questions for the entire test varies from 30-60 questions, depending on the difficulty. 3-8 papers will be sent approximately 10 days before the written entrance test to the applicants.</p>
    <p>Example:</p>
    <p>The authors assume similar loyalty intentions for potential customers.</p>
    <p>A.) True</p>
    <p>B.) False</p>

